# The status panel on the main screen (StatusWin, see statuswin.c): the square the panel is looking at, in the box at the lower
# left (its picture and the lines under it). The mouse can't be moved over the squares one at a time (the console only moves
# the panel with the cursor), so the scene points the panel at squares by hand (host status_look dx dy, relative to the first unit's
# square) and changes the squares' records (host status_tile dx dy OFFSET VALUE; offset bit 8 sets bits, bit 9 clears them, bit 10 sets
# one byte; 0 and 4 are the climate/contour/site/region and visibility/rock/territory words, 8 and 12 the bits and landmark words).
# This scene is the terrain lines: ocean and land, altitude, rainfall, rockiness, the river, fungus and forest, flooding and the
# climate change, the improvements, a monolith, a resource and the landmarks, the square never seen, and the debug flags.
# The panel's fields (the state regions sw_*: the camera, the fonts without their handles, the square and picks, the Spot list's counts) and the text buffer are compared with every snap.
